  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nThe synoptic pattern set-up of high pressure aloft building over\nthe South, while surface high pressure to the east keeps a pump\nof warm/moist return flow here, translates to dangerously\nhot/humid conditions for us the first half of this new week.\nHI's peak daily around/in excess of 100 degrees, and may climb\nupwards locally to near 110 degrees on the hottest days, \nMonday-Tuesday.\n\nStorm chances return over the back half of the week. The best\nand most widespread chance, including strong storm chances, is \nThursday, when a sharp, positively-tilted trof tracks from the \nGreat Lakes to the Upper Ohio Valley. Best severe and heavy rain\nchances do appear to be closer to the synoptic center of the\nsystem, which would keep such chances mostly focused to our \nnorth and east.",
